response:
To terminate a C program, you can use the `exit()` function from the standard library (`stdlib.h`). This will immediately end your program's execution.

Here is an example of how to use it:

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
    printf("Hello World!\n");

    // Terminate the program with exit code 0 (success)
    exit(0);
}
```

In this case, when the program reaches the line containing `exit(0);`, it stops executing further lines in the current scope or any nested scopes within that point onward.
